    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455-a2">

                <pb facs="0884" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg760"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Appendix to inclosure in No. 124.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santa Fé, N. Mex.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 9,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Assistant
                        Adjutant-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Fort Leavenworth,
                        Kans.:</hi></p>
                <p>The following just received from General Hatch, dated Fort Bliss, Texas, March
                    8;</p>
                <p>“Inform department headquarters, Terrasas is at Carrisal with 200 men operating
                    against hostile Indians. The garrison at El Paso, Mexico, has 370 regular
                    Mexican troops. I have ordered Indian companies and detachments with cavalry to
                    Mexican line, keeping out strong patrols east of Fort Cummings. If the Mexican
                    troops drive the Indians north will make every effort to strike them.”</p>
                <closer><signed>LOUD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Assistant
                            Adjutant-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
